( **click for map image**), located on the deck of the boat docked in the Combine Dredge._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n_Say \"slow\" to request the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Mewes'\nCaptain Mewes says 'Shhhhhhh. Don't let [them] see you talking to me.'\nYou say, 'Who is 'them'?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'Those horrible Doomscale. They do such dreadful things to me, but I can [explain] later. I have some [tasks] for you if you want to help me stick a [wrench] in their work, but you can't let them know I sent you. If you are in a hurry and don't want to hear me prattle on, I need you to [disrupt] their rest, [slow] their mining, and [hamper] their research.'\nYou say, 'A wrench?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'I have some subtle sabotage [tasks] for you. ...Okay, they're not that subtle at all. I just hope she won't make me do those [horrible] things if her attention is drawn elsewhere.'\nYou say, 'What tasks?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'I would like to disrupt their [rest], slow their [mining], and hamper their [research]. Will you help me?'\nYou say, 'What about the mining?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The Combine used this area as a mining platform ages ago. They recently started using it again shortly before Lanys and her toadies came and forcefully took it over. It was [awful]. While Lanys allows them most of the product of the mining, she takes some and has them working on some [other] task. But enough prattling on. I need you to [slow] their mining with some judicious sabotage.'\nYou say, 'What was awful?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The Combine attacked everyone on the boat, but they were not prepared for Lanys and the Doomscale. It was a slaughter. Ten members of the Combine were slain for every Doomscale that fell. And it was a sight to behold when Lanys defeated half of the Combine single-handedly.'\nYou say, 'I'll slow them down...'\nCaptain Mewes says 'Thank you. I have written what you need to do in your journal, but if you like I can tell you more about the [sabotage].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Undermining the Mining'.\nCaptain Mewes is not happy about his treatment. He wants you to complete tasks to disrupt the Doomscale and Combine efforts. For this task he wants you to hamper their ability to process ore.\nYou say, 'Tell me about the sabotage'\nCaptain Mewes says 'Go to the [rock quarry] and destroy some of the [elementari] and [operari] there. Afterwards, move on to the [ore processing platform] and make your way inside. At the top, you will find some of the operari processing ore. Destroy some of them, and damage a few of the ore processing kilns by putting a [heat resistant] explosive from the bundle inside. If you lose the [bundle], come back to me and tell me. I will give you another. Please don't waste them as I have a difficult time getting them. When you are done, kill a few [Doomscale] on your way back to me.'\nYou say, 'Where is the rock quarry?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The rock quarry is to the northeast. Take the north path between the two exits from the dock. Pass under the housing platform and take the northeastern path past it. Stay to the left, and when you reach a dead end, activate the geomantic elevator to raise some of the seabed to cross over to the quarry.'\nYou say, 'What are the elementari?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The elementari are three-legged abominations of rock, created by the geomancers. You'll find most of them at the quarry.'\nYou say, 'What are the operari?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The operari are golem like creatures created by the Combine as laborers. They do not create them here, but replacements are shipped in from time to time.'\nYou say, 'Where is the ore processing platform?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The ore processing platform is west of the quarry. Take the west path out of the quarry and it will lead you right to it.'\nYou say, 'What is this heat resistant thing?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'The explosive is in a heat-resistant wrapper. Note that I said heat-resistant, not heatproof. After about five seconds the heat-resistant wrapper will burn away in the kiln, and the contents will explode. Though this explosion is small, you should step away from the kiln to avoid being injured. Also, the operari are very resilient and will not be damaged by this explosion, though you're likely to have already fought them in order to gain access to the kiln.'\nYou say, 'What bundle are you talking about?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'Look. I appreciate your help, but you already have a bundle of explosives. I'm not responsible if you left it in a bank, somewhere else, or you misplaced it in your copious bags. I can't afford to give you another if you already have one.'\nYou say, 'What about the Doomscale?'\nCaptain Mewes says 'I don't care which Doomscale you kill, as long as you make Lanys' life difficult by doing so.'\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nMake your way to the rock quarry 0/1 (Combine Dredge)\n_Location update at about /loc 1540, -1150, -30 (the quarry is a large area in the northeastern part of the zone)._\nKill elementari and operari 0/6 (Combine Dredge)\n_Kill six mobs with \"elementari\" or \"operari\" in their names._\n\n---\n\nMake your way to the ore processing platform 0/1 (Combine Dredge)\n_Location update at about /loc 1380, -470, 40 (this is the northernmost of the spiral towers)._\nKill operari 0/2 (Combine Dredge)\n_Kill two mobs with \"operari\" in their names._\nSabotage the ore processing kilns 0/5 (Combine Dredge)\n_Use the \"Fire Resistant Explosive Bundle\" (received at the beginning of the task) near kilns (kilns are located in each room of the top floor of this tower). This causes an explosion, so move away from it after you set it._\nKill 20 Doomscales 0/20 (Combine Dredge)\n_Kill any 20 \"Doomscale\" mobs._\n\n---\n\nReport success to Captain Mewes 0/1 (Combine Dredge)\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n150 platinum",
